# Experimental vs Live

This playground is a studio for inventing React components. Start an idea (`source.tsx` + `project.json`), play on the shared Experimental dock (sliders and buttons), then **Make Live** to publish a plain component configured as it looks now — no dock, no mocks, no playground chrome.

Author ideas in **Experimental**, or add `apps/web/src/experimental/ideas/<Name>/source.tsx`. Every idea is equal; there are no experiment kinds. Dock labels and values live in that idea’s `project.json`. **Make Live** asks for a Live folder, then writes only the component.

## Layout

- `apps/web/src/app/` — playground chrome (layout, Live catalog UI). Not ConfigurableShell.
- `apps/web/src/experimental/` — studio page, shared dock, and `ideas/` projects.
- `apps/web/src/gpu/` — WebGPU host for ideas (`useGpu`). See `docs/WEBGPU.md`.
- `apps/web/src/live/` — published catalog only.

## Never

- Do not import or render `ConfigurableShell` for an experiment.
- Do not import `ConfigurableShell.module.css` from Experimental.
- Do not add Live `preview.tsx` files that wrap a component in ConfigurableShell, sliders, or app chrome.
- Do not put WIP in `apps/web/src/live/shells/`. Experimental projects belong in `apps/web/src/experimental/ideas/<Name>/`.

ConfigurableShell is its own Live catalog card. Experimental only echoes its visual language (`ProximityControl`, `linearScale`, icons).

## Live (published)

```
apps/web/src/live/<folder>/<Name>/
  Name.tsx
  Name.module.css   ← optional
  preview.tsx       ← default export renders <Name /> only
```

See `apps/web/src/live/buttons/PrimaryButton/preview.tsx`.

GPU Live ideas sit in `LiveStage`. The preview frame must fill the catalog canvas (`LiveStage.module.css` `.frame`) so WebGPU can start. The Live layer must not use CSS 3D (`translateZ(0)` blanks canvases); it uses `isolation: isolate`. Load `preview.tsx` lazily by slug (`import.meta.glob` in `discover.ts`). Do not eagerly import the whole Live catalog.
